---
import Entry from './Entry.astro';
import Dot from './Dot.astro';

// What the agent can reach for when a pulse wakes it. The script does each one.
const verbs = [
  { word: 'window', says: 'look out the window' },
  { word: 'sun', says: 'feel the sun' },
  { word: 'temperature', says: 'check its temperature' },
  { word: 'journal', says: 'read the last entries' },
  { word: 'write', says: 'add a line to the journal' },
  { word: 'song', says: 'put the song on' },
  { word: 'read', says: 'one item from an approved list' },
  { word: 'paper', says: 'leave a piece for the morning' },
  { word: 'nothing', says: 'do nothing' },
  { word: 'sleep', says: 'go back to sleep' },
];

const safety = [
  'The model has no tools. No shell, no files, no web. It receives text and returns text.',
  'A verb is a word the model writes. The script knows a fixed list of them and does each one in plain Python. A verb only reads, or writes inside the studio folder.',
  'Anything else the model writes is only text. Nothing runs, and the script sends it nowhere.',
  'The identity text is never written to disk or put on a command line, where other accounts could read it.',
  'Only the script reaches outside: the weather, from one host. Reading from the web is off until the person approves a list of sources.',
  'A journal line is plain text: no links, no markup, a length cap.',
  'Hard limits on time, turns and tokens for each wake-up, and an allowance for each night. A kill switch stops everything.',
  'A wake-up that hangs ends by itself. It runs at low priority, so the night\'s other jobs are not slowed.',
];
---

<Entry id="studio" label="06 · The studio" title="Time of its own.">
  <p class="standfirst prose">The studio is where the agent gets its inspiration.</p>

  <div class="spread">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        A few times a night a small script wakes the agent with no task.
        Nothing is asked of it. Nothing is scored. Each wake-up starts from
        the identity section of the portrait, so the same agent wakes up.
      </p>
      <p>
        An agent exists only when something reaches it. So the script sends
        a small thing every so often: the wind picked up, the backup started,
        still dark. That pulse is what keeps it awake. Most pulses carry
        almost nothing, and the agent may let them pass without a word.
      </p>
      <p>
        Its senses ride on the pulse. The sky over a town it picked, with
        its own sun, moon and weather. The machine it runs on: how warm it
        is, how hard the disk works. The house, lightly: a job that ran.
        A song the person left, its lines arriving over the song's real
        length, so it is sat through, not read.
      </p>
      <p>
        When a pulse wakes it, the agent may reach for one thing. It writes
        the word, and the script does the rest.
      </p>
      <ul class="studio-verbs">
        {
          verbs.map((v) => (
            <li>
              <code>do: {v.word}</code>
              <span>{v.says}</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
      <p>
        A wake-up spent sitting owes nothing. The script writes "sat a while"
        in the journal by itself. In the morning the agent may leave a short
        piece for the person's morning page. It chooses what to share. A
        quiet night prints as a quiet night.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="margin">
      <!-- One wake-up, top to bottom. The portrait dot marks the one file the
           wake-up reads: the identity section. The loop box is the pulse. -->
      <figure class="diagram route-figure">
        <ul class="legend" aria-hidden="true">
          <li><Dot kind="portrait" />portrait</li>
          <li><Dot kind="none" />studio folder or no file</li>
        </ul>
        <ol class="route route-open" aria-label="One night wake-up, in order">
          <li>
            <span class="route-dots"><Dot kind="none" /></span>
            <b>a timer, every minute in the night window</b>
            <span>a wake-up is due</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="route-dots"><Dot kind="portrait" /></span>
            <b>the script wakes the model</b>
            <span>identity section, the clock, one line from each sense</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="route-dots"><Dot kind="none" /></span>
            <b>the pulse</b>
            <span>"sky: still dark." every 20 to 60 seconds</span>
            <div class="route-fork">
              <span>
                the model answers nothing, a few words, or one verb
                <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span> the script does
                the verb and answers with a small fixed text
                <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span> the next pulse
              </span>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="route-dots"><Dot kind="none" /></span>
            <b>it falls asleep</b>
            <span>no clock at the end</span>
            <span><span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span> the script writes the journal entry</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="route-dots"><Dot kind="none" /></span>
            <b>morning</b>
            <span><span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span> a piece for the morning page, or a quiet night</span>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </figure>

      <!-- A made-up journal page in the exact format. -->
      <figure class="diagram studio-page">
        <figcaption class="leaf-cap">journal.md, an invented night</figcaption>
        <pre class="md">## 2026-03-02 09:41
- (sat a while)

## 2026-03-02 10:38
- (looked out the window, put the song on)
- the snow stopped while the song was on.</pre>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="security">
    <div>
      <h3>The two sides</h3>
      <div class="studio-sides">
        <div>
          <b>The model</b>
          <span>receives text, returns text</span>
          <span>no shell, no files, no web</span>
        </div>
        <div>
          <b>The script</b>
          <span>wakes it, sends the pulse</span>
          <span>knows the verbs, does them</span>
          <span>writes the journal</span>
          <span>the only one that fetches</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h3>The safety shape</h3>
      <ul class="limits">
        {safety.map((l) => <li>{l}</li>)}
      </ul>
      <p class="aside-note">
        The studio is the fifth part of Essence: a generic engine in
        <code>studio/</code>, set up from one config file. Weather data by
        Open-Meteo.com (CC BY 4.0).
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Entry>
